   1133  fd39							; Door stripe color ($8D) is staged inside PhaseBlink (this window
   1134  fd39							; was full to the $F4C4 pin, retired 2026-10-20 — the 14B staging
   1135  fd39							; block lives with the walk where there is hole).
   1136  fd39							; --- Phase 3: phase-cell blink (PF buffer pokes) ----------------------
   1137  fd39							; Body moved after the level data (PhaseBlink, ~130B — the StageBandTab
   1138  fd39							; window $F3C4..$F4C4 was full; the data window has the only free
   1139  fd39							; hole). Contract: clobbers A/X/Y/FetchPtr/RectCount/LineCount/
   1140  fd39							; CollisionCellX/CollisionEndY ($8F scratch — the pack below rebuilds
   1141  fd39							; it). The PF buffers ARE the collision map (cell walk + laser read
   1142  fd39							; them) — toggling the cell's two bits THERE makes render + PHM +
   1143  fd39							; laser follow with zero kernel cost. 64f full cycle = EnemyRamP bit5
   1144  fd39							; (32 on + 32 off; clock-derived, no state bytes — locked plan).
   1145  fd39							; --- PhaseBlink ping-pong (chunk A2): it MUST run after the band/ball
   1146  fd39							; staging above and before the pack below (the crunch walk overwrites
   1147  fd39							; Temp/BandTab for its cell — running it earlier let SBT's own staging
